  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts with a seeded LCG that scatters 8,000 trees and 2,000 rocks over a radius-60 disc. The scene has a ground plane and three instanced draws: `instances.cylinder` for trunks, `instances.cone` for canopies and `instances.sphere` for rocks. Canopies and rocks get per-instance HSL colours on a white base material. One shadow-casting directional light has its shadow fit to the forest. The scene also has exponential fog and a hemisphere light. The camera is `camera.orbit` with `autoRotate` 0.12 rad/s, placed so the whole forest is in view. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on a `requestAnimationFrame` after the first `onFrame` callback. Typecheck passes. I could not run `vite build` or load the page here. So I haven't seen the render, and I haven't confirmed that the shadows work or that the auto-rotating camera moves.",
